From d767b6767fc55c7a4ade99ea3255cd85194130bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 22:05:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Gatekeeper: default-deny device access control (reaper
 v1.6.8)

New opt-in feature (off by default). Unknown devices joining the LAN are
held at the gate - no internet AND no access to other LAN devices - until
the owner approves them. Four per-device states: full, internet-only,
guest (internet-only + timed expiry), blocked. Enabling snapshots the
devices already present as approved so nothing breaks at turn-on.

Enforcement (rc/gatekeeper.c writes an idempotent /tmp/gk/apply.sh):
- iptables/ip6tables FORWARD REAPER_GKF : internet gate (approved RETURN,
  else DROP; hooked at position 1 so a revocation beats any ESTABLISHED
  shortcut; fc flush on every apply so offloaded flows re-traverse)
- iptables/ip6tables INPUT REAPER_GKI : router-services gate (a held
  device may reach only DHCP/DNS/HTTP-captive; fences the admin UI off)
- iptables nat PREROUTING REAPER_GKN : tcp/80 DNAT to httpd for the
  captive "awaiting approval" page (OS captive probes are plain HTTP)
- ebtables FORWARD REAPER_GK : LAN isolation at the bridge (only
  approved-FULL MACs source bridged frames; internet-only/guest/blocked/
  unknown cannot see, scan or ARP other LAN devices)
Re-applied from start_firewall (chains just rebuilt) and self-healed by
gkd after the lan/wireless/dnsmq/wanduck ebtables -F flushes.

gkd (new daemon, obj-y, no listener): ARP + IPv6-neigh + DHCP-lease +
per-BSS assoclist discovery -> /tmp/gk/seen.tsv for the UI; syslogs first
sight of a new MAC (gk_notify); expires guest passes; self-heals rules.

httpd: reaper_gk.cgi (do_auth, http_id CSRF) status/set/remove/config +
enable-time baseline snapshot; pre-auth captive intercept in handle_request
serves a self-contained waiting page to unapproved MACs in quarantine mode.

UI: Reaper_GK.asp (reaper-native) - master toggle, summary strip, pending
approvals, device table with per-row state control, settings, captive
preview, honest limits. Own left-rail entry (menuTree + dashboard rail).
RGK_00-56 in all 25 dicts (EN seeded across all; real translations owed).

nvram (defaults.c): gk_enable/gk_default/gk_guest_hours/gk_captive/
gk_notify (all off/safe defaults) + gk_rl (CKN_STR_MAX device list).
EBTABLES userspace already =y in config_rt-be96u.

HONEST LIMIT baked into the page + docs: a MAC is identity not auth
(spoofable behind WPA) - defense in depth, not a first wall. METAL PROBE
OWED before claiming intra-SSID isolation: same-BSS client-to-client
traffic may be bridged inside the Broadcom driver below ebtables.

Version bumped to Reaper_v1.6.8.
