+RGK_41=Turning Gatekeeper on trusts everything already here. Every device on your network at that moment is approved automatically, so nothing you own breaks.
+RGK_42=Quarantine blocks both directions: a held device cannot reach the internet and cannot see, scan, or talk to your other devices. Internet-only mode keeps the LAN side sealed permanently &mdash; right for cameras, TVs, and smart-home gear.
+RGK_43=This is a second wall, not the first. A MAC address is identity, not proof &mdash; someone who already has your Wi-Fi password could imitate an approved device. Gatekeeper stops rogue gadgets, shared-password guests, and anything plugged into an open port.
+RGK_44=Phones using a rotating private address may reappear as new devices; the pending list flags them so you know what you are looking at.
